==Strategy==
==='''Chapter 1'''===
The Face is the strongest enemy faced up to this point, but is hampered by several weaknesses which make him a pushover - low movement speed, slow attack rate, and somewhat mediocre range. Overall, The Face is very easy if you have most of the available [[Treasure]]s unlocked.

Begin the battle by spawning a couple of [[Cat (Normal Cat)|Macho Cats]], [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Wall Cats]], [[Gross Cat (Normal Cat)|Sexy Legs Cats]] and [[Bird Cat (Normal Cat)|UFO Cats]]. Meanwhile, upgrade your [[Worker Cat]] to max level. Once the first step has been completed, wait for your wallet to fill up. It should not take long due to the enemies that will give lots of cash. Now you can start to spam [[Gross Cat (Normal Cat)|Sexy Legs Cats]], [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Dragon Cats]] and [[Titan Cat (Normal Cat)| Mythical Titan Cats]] alongside your meatshields (Macho and Wall). If you have a lot of money stored, then try to spawn lots of UFO Cats as well. Don't freak out when Kang Roo will appear, she will not be a problem as your meatshields will prevent her from moving forward. If these steps were followed correctly, The Face will die easily. Proceed to the enemy base, and victory will be in your grasp. Note: this stage is EXTREMELY EASY and almost no strategy is required to beat it. Remember that Wall and Macho can protect your ranged units like Dragon and Sexy Legs.

==='''Chapter 2'''===
Dark Emperor Nyandam is another slow enemy, but more importantly, his attack rate is not that fast either, making him fairly easy and similar to The Face. Unlike The Face, he has the range to hit all [[:Category:Normal Cats|Normal Cats]] and purchasable [[:Category:Special Cats|Special Cats]], preventing you from just stacking [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Dragon Cats]]. Prepare a lineup with all [[:Category:Anti-Red Cats|anti-Red cats]] you own, as well as other Normal Cats. The One Horn cycles are generally the hardest part of the stage, so it is highly recommended to bring [[Fish Cat (Normal Cat)|Whale Cat]] no matter your lineup. Above all, however, [[Treasure]]s are the most important thing to have.

An especially easy way to beat him is through [[:Category:Cats with Knockback ability|cats with knockback abilities]] against [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]] enemies. If Dark Emperor Nyandam is by the enemy base, knockback will continually stun the boss and prevent him from attacking. [[Pirate Cat (Rare Cat)|Pirate Cat]] is the definitive choice for this strategy, but [[Bean Cats (Special Cat)|Bean Cats]], [[Raiden (Uber Rare Cat)|Raiden]] and some other units are also workable.

Keep in mind that, due to Dark Emperor Nyandam's slow attacks, any important unit should be summoned just after he attacks, so they'll stay alive as long as possible. You can also further delay Nyandam's attacks by using the [[Cat Cannon]] right before he does an attack to get a little bit of extra time.

At this point is time it is not really required to get treasures but they can help. If you are struggling with this stage, evolve Fish Cat into Whale Cat and use Whale as your main attacker and tanker for the boss.

==='''Chapter 3'''===
This stage is radically different than the others, featuring a fast-attacking and short-ranged enemy as the boss. Learning to meatshield is mandatory, and so is getting at least the most important [[Treasure]]s from all three chapters. Any [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber]] or [[:Category:Legend Rare Cats|Legend Rare]] you have by now, if you have any, is likely to help, while close-ranged attackers like [[Bird Cat (Normal Cat)|UFO Cat]], [[Fish Cat (Normal Cat)|Whale Cat]] and [[Titan Cat (Normal Cat)|Mythical Titan Cat]] become a waste of money.

The general strategy is to stack massive amounts of long-ranged attackers on Teacher Bun Bun (anything with over 200 range will be safe), while sending out "meatshield" units such as [[Cat (Normal Cat)|Macho Cat]] and [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Wall Cat]] non-stop to keep them well-protected. The stage can be won using only [[:Category:Normal Cats|Normal Cats]] and [[Valkyrie Cat (Special Cat)|Valkyrie Cat]], but adding [[Boogie Cat (Special Cat)|Boogie Cat]] or any other cat with the same level of spammability ([[Gold Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Gold Cat]], [[Catburger (Special Cat)|Catburger]], [[Awa-Odori Cat (Rare Cat)|Awa-Odori Cat]], [[Pumpcat (Rare Cat)|Pumpcat]], etc.) will make things vastly easier. Luring Teacher Bun Bun close to the [[Cat Base]] is not as risky as it sounds, and is recommended if the support enemies keep getting in the way.

Gacha units such as [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Paris Cat]] and [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Sadako Cat]] make this stage much easier.

