==Trivia==
*In [[Nyanko Daisensou|BCJP]], this is the only [[Empire of Cats]] stage not to take place in one of the prefectures of Japan, since all 47 are already conquered in the previous stages. Instead, it takes place on the second-largest island in Okinawa Prefecture, '''Iriomote Island'', the only place where [[wikipedia:Iriomote cat|Iriomote cats]] can be found.
**The base being a tree with a sign reading "embrace the wilderness" makes more sense in the context of Iriomote Island than the Moon, as the island is mostly unexplored and is 90% jungles and swamps.
**Iriomote Island is one of the two stages in the game to change [[Backgrounds|background]] between chapters, the other being [[Dubai (Into the Future)|Dubai]] in [[Into the Future]]. In Chapters 1 and 3 it uses the dawn overworld background, while Chapter 2 takes place at night.
*The text on the Japanese version's base says "野生の底力" (yasei no sokojikara), meaning "underlying strength of the wild" or "underlying strength of the wilderness".
*Moon and [[Japan (Empire of Cats)|Japan]] are the only Empire of Cats stages whose enemy bases in [[The Battle Cats|BCEN]] aren't taken from [[Kumanchu Royale]], as the Moon instead uses an English-localized version of Iriomote Island's base (a tree) from BCJP, leaving the original Moon base unused. In [[The Battle Cats POP!]], however, the Moon stage uses a similar but shorter version of the one from Kumanchu Royale.
*It is the only Empire of Cats stage to play out differently in each chapter.
*Each non-[[Zombie Outbreaks|Outbreak]] version of this stage has a remake in a different [[Legend Stages]] campaign. Chapter 1 has [[Cricket Ideology]] in [[Uncanny Legends]], Chapter 2 has [[Pointless Pauldrons]] in [[Zero Legends]], and Chapter 3 has [[Warrior's Dawn]] in [[Stories of Legend]].

